# SupraLINUX KCalendarCore source/package notes

KDE upstream v6.30.0 is the authority for source, features and build requirements.
Source: https://download.kde.org/stable/frameworks/6.30/kcalendarcore-6.30.0.tar.xz
Source SHA-256: e8bf60e398e2f8098a4db7db44c5475d70540ad8f8948a123c8bc109dc4db776
Upstream root CMakeLists Git blob: 0414c1256b209ae14c41f2ccc0a99480f3298a17

Batch 7 preserves the KDE 6.30 Linux/shared-library defaults: Python bindings and
tests are enabled; KWidgetsAddons also keeps its Designer plugin enabled. The
explicit ON flags in debian/rules mirror the verified upstream 6.30 defaults and
make accidental feature loss fail closed. QCH remains disabled only under the
already-established common SupraLINUX Frameworks package profile.

Python installation uses DEB_PYTHON_INSTALL_LAYOUT=deb so ECM sysconfig installs
the extension under /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages rather than /usr/local.

Debian 6.28.0 packaging is retained only as a technical compatibility reference
for public symbols, package split conventions and copyright metadata.
Packaging-tree evidence: run 34708030450, artifact 10301938362.
Symbols baseline SHA-256: 2662789d8c2e5715f218e40826a15a261a151bfda2d2695e5c5efefbc2d26127
